## Skills repository rules

This part is generated by skenv from the repository harness ([[ .Harness ]]);
local instructions go outside this block.

### Layout

- One skill per directory `skills/<name>/` with `SKILL.md` (Agent Skills
  format, agentskills.io): YAML frontmatter with `name` (equal to the
  directory name, `[a-z0-9-]`, at most 64 characters) and `description`
  (at most 1024 characters); `license` is a top-level field, `metadata` a
  map of strings (`metadata.source` says where the content comes from).
- Supporting files: `references/*.md`, `scripts/`, `assets/`. Links in
  `SKILL.md` and `references/*.md` are relative and stay inside the skill.
- Optional tests: an executable `skills/<name>/check`. CI and the pre-push
  hook run it from the skill directory for every changed skill, with
  `CHECK_PYTHON` / `UV_PYTHON` set to 3.9 and 3.12 in CI.

### Creating a skill

1. `mkdir -p skills/<name>` and write `SKILL.md` with the frontmatter above.
2. `skenv lint skills/<name>` until it is clean.
3. Add `check` if the skill has scripts; executables need a shebang.

### Checking

- `skenv lint` (all skills) or `skenv lint --staged`: rules L1–L6
  (frontmatter, name, limits, relative links, file size and secret-like
  files, shebangs).
- `lefthook install` once: pre-commit runs `skenv lint --staged`, ruff,
  shellcheck and gitleaks on staged files; pre-push runs `check` of changed
  skills.
- CI (`.github/workflows/check.yml`): `skenv repo check`, `skenv lint`,
  ruff, pyright, shellcheck, markdownlint, gitleaks and the skill checks.
- Managed files (first line `managed by skenv … — do not edit`) and the
  `skenv:begin/end` blocks are regenerated by `skenv repo apply`; change the
  templates in skenv instead of editing them. `skenv repo check` fails on
  any drift.

### Secrets and publication

- No secrets, tokens, keys or `.env` files in skills, history or CI logs.
- Nothing moves to a public repository without the publication check
  (license, `metadata.source`, stop-list, gitleaks over the whole history).
- Do not add `CLAUDE.md` or `.claude/CLAUDE.md`: in Claude Code's default
  mode it disables loading of this `AGENTS.md`.
